(Classification of three-dimensional shrinking solitons). Let \( \left( {M,{g}_{ij}\left( t\right) }\right) \) be a nonflat gradient shrinking soliton on a three-manifold. Suppose \( \left( {M,{g}_{ij}\left( t\right) }\right) \) has bounded and nonnegative sectional curvature and is \( \kappa \) -noncollapsed on all scales for some \( \kappa  > 0 \) . Then \( \left( {M,{g}_{ij}\left( t\right) }\right) \) is one of the following:

(i) the round three-sphere \( {\mathbb{S}}^{3} \) , or a metric quotient of \( {\mathbb{S}}^{3} \) ;

(ii) the round infinite cylinder \( {\mathbb{S}}^{2} \times  \mathbb{R} \) , or one of its \( {\mathbb{Z}}_{2} \) quotients.
